==Special attack==
The Tonalztics of Ralos has a [[special attack]], ''Division'', costing 50% special attack energy. ''Division'' increases accuracy by 50% and reduces the target's [[Defence]] level by 1/8 of the target's [[Magic]] level upon a [[successful hit]]. This effect occurs for each individual hit, meaning a ''charged'' special attack can potentially reduce the target's defence twice ''(1/4 of Magic level)''.

This effect makes it uniquely useful for high-defence targets who have an accompanying high-magic level, or for draining the defence of targets who are otherwise unreachable with standard methods (like a [[dragon warhammer]]), provided that their light ranged defence is relatively low. The weapon shines best against enemies such as [[Zulrah]], the [[Great Olm]], and [[The Maiden of Sugadinti]], as these enemies have high Magic levels with little or no light ranged defence.

When used on NPCs, the defence reduction from a successful first hit will apply for the calculation of the second hit. However, this is not the case when used in PvP.{{CiteTwitter|url=https://x.com/jagexash/status/1794310805233840131|date=25 May 2024|author=Mod Ash|archiveurl=https://archive.is/uEGYt|archivedate=30 May 2024|quote=On an NPC, I believe any defence reduction from the 1st calculated hit can help with the 2nd roll even though it's in the same tick. However, on a player, I *believe* the target's effective defence would not be recalculated within that tick, so the 2nd roll may not be helped.}}

The special attack animation differs depending on whether the weapon is charged.

