==Trivia==
* The weapon was initially proposed as the "Glaive of Ralos" but was changed to its current name after player feedback. The term "{{wp|glaive}}" historically refers to a polearmed weapon, and was popularised as a term describing thrown weapons that return to the user after the 1983 film ''{{wp|Krull (film)|Krull}},'' which features a similarly shaped weapon as its {{wp|MacGuffin}}. Indeed, ''RuneScape 3'' also has a similarly named weapon, the {{RSL|shadow glaive}}, as well as a proper glaive named the {{RSL|Death Lotus Glaive}}.
* The word "tonalztics" is made up of morphemes from the {{wp|Nahuatl}} language. The root "tona-" evokes the warmth of the Sun, as in {{wp|Tōnatiuh}}, a deity who carries the Sun across the sky, or {{wp|tonalli}}, an animating force and aspect of one's soul that manifests in one way as internal body temperature. Many Nahuatl nouns and adjectives end in "-ztic".
* Unlike most stat-reducing special attack weapons, which can apply their draining effects on an accurate hit that does not deal damage, the Tonalztics of Ralos requires a specific check for damage to be dealt. Targets with attack-type specific damage reduction such as the Great Olm's Left Hand thus requires a minimum hit of 1 damage to apply draining effects. {{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/431834766325841920/1529141679318368409|date=21 July 2026|quote=|ctxquote=|archiveurl=|archivedate=|notes=|name=|group=}}

